  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is atorvastatin. A human comparative PK table directly reports atorvastatin oral bioavailability as 14%, below the 20% threshold. Although some related statins show higher bioavailability, their different core structures and first-pass metabolism limit transferability; the direct atorvastatin value is decisive. Prediction: low.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No dedicated atorvastatin absolute bioavailability study record is present; the 14% value comes from a comparative table without dose/formulation details.",
    "High-bioavailability statin analogues such as fluvastatin and cerivastatin have different core structures, limiting quantitative transfer to atorvastatin.",
    "Prediction relies on identifying the query as atorvastatin and using a comparative table entry rather than a query-specific PK record."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

